  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="ea4f-98f8-637c-f13d" name="Hittite Empire (Chariot Wars) - List Notes" publicationId="513c-2d0a-024a-da5a" hidden="false">
      <description>HITTITE EMPIRE ARMY LIST (Chariot Wars, pp.25-32), 1600 BC to 800 BC. Also used for Hurrian (Mitanni), Syrian, Canaanite, Phoenician and Hyksos armies, Arzawa, and (with modification) the Neo-Hittite successor states.
Characters up to 25%; at least one character to command. A small army of 1,000 points can be commanded by a Senior Officer (or Vassal King) rather than a General (Great King, Prince or Ally King). Chariotry at least 25%. Infantry at least 25%. Allies &amp; Mercenaries up to HALF the points value of the army.
Chariot Runners: one unit per unit of two-crew chariots. The cavalry unit is 0-1 (Scout Cavalry or Hittite Successor Cavalry).

ARMY COMPOSITIONS:
[Hittite Empire]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Chariotry: at least 25%
  Infantry: at least 25%
  Allies &amp; Mercenaries: up to 50%
  Standard composition.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
